# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE RULE, as of v19.6.0: track what something else needs in order to RUN, plus the
# provenance record of a result. Everything derived stays out.
#
#   output/estimates/   TRACKED   the bundles and their CSV siblings. Hours of compute,
#                                 not regenerable, and read by every downstream script.
#   output/logs/        TRACKED   nothing needs a log to run, but a log is the only record
#                                 of what a run did, and a bundle without its log is a
#                                 parameter vector with no history. Same commit as the
#                                 bundle it describes.
#   output/transition/  TRACKED   read by plots_and_tables/transition.jl.
#   output/chains/      ignored   draw arrays. Once the standard errors are sealed into the
#                                 estimate bundle nothing needs them for a TABLE — but as of
#                                 v19.8.0 they also carry chain_lp and the accepted/replaced
#                                 masks, which are what lets the estimator be changed later
#                                 without re-running. ~200 MB at N=95, gens=10 000. Keep the
#                                 file; it is the run, not a derivative of it.
#   output/plots/       ignored   derived, in full.
#   output/tables/      ignored   derived, in full.
#
# A NOTE ON RULES THAT NEVER BIT. Before v19.6.0 four paths carried ignore rules, or were
# assumed ignored, and were tracked anyway — a rule cannot untrack a path already in the
# index. code/notebooks (37 files), code/single_run_plots_all (20), output/tables (9) and
# output/plots (191). The `git rm --cached` in the v19.6.0 restructure is what made them
# effective.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/extra documents/
/literature/
/data/raw/
/data/derived/*.arrow
/latex/
literature.zip

/code/roysearch_v*/
/code/roysearch_v*.zip
/code/notebooks/
/code/single_run_plots_all/
/code/.vscode/
/code/.ipynb_checkpoints/

/output/plots/
/output/tables/
/output/chains/

# Migration staging. migrate_bundles.jl and the v19.6.0 relocation stage here, at the repo
# root and OUTSIDE output/, and remove it on success: a migration that succeeds leaves
# nothing, one that fails leaves everything. The rules that used to hide migration traces
# inside output/smm/ (_migration/, *.jls.pre_migration, *.jls.pre_vm) are gone with the
# directory — a trace that has to be hidden is a trace that should not have been written.
/.migration/

.DS_Store
